1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
The gallery has filled
up since episode eleven.

2
00:00:02,818 --> 00:00:07,698
Today I'm shopping for a 2026
planner for my reMarkable Paper Pro.

3
00:00:07,783 --> 00:00:11,703
We'll narrow the gallery down, judge
what's left, and take one home.

4
00:00:11,925 --> 00:00:14,935
These controls sit above
every gallery view.

5
00:00:15,036 --> 00:00:16,736
Category comes first.

6
00:00:16,803 --> 00:00:21,860
Nobody files anything here: the gallery
works out each project's category from its

7
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:22,973
tags and name.

8
00:00:23,117 --> 00:00:24,107
Planners.

9
00:00:27,019 --> 00:00:29,919
Size or device matters most for a tablet.

10
00:00:30,043 --> 00:00:33,743
Some entries cover several
devices that share a screen,

11
00:00:33,743 --> 00:00:37,693
like the 10.3-inch one, because
one file fits them all.

12
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:39,330
Mine's the Paper Pro.

13
00:00:41,036 --> 00:00:46,016
Results start sorted by Trending: what
people are opening and forking lately.

14
00:00:46,128 --> 00:00:48,628
Newest and Most downloaded are here too.

15
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:52,494
Top rated weighs each average
by how many reviews back it,

16
00:00:52,494 --> 00:00:56,778
so one lucky five-star review
can't outrank lots of good ones.

17
00:00:56,996 --> 00:01:00,426
4+ keeps projects averaging
four stars or more.

18
00:01:00,489 --> 00:01:04,509
Notice what else drops out:
anything nobody has rated yet.

19
00:01:04,714 --> 00:01:10,444
List view puts the same results in a table,
so sizes and ratings sit side by side.

20
00:01:10,649 --> 00:01:14,035
Everything I've picked is
written into the page's address.

21
00:01:14,081 --> 00:01:19,661
Bookmark it, or send it to a friend, and it
opens this exact list, signed in or not.

22
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:22,587
Back in the grid, tags are filters too.

23
00:01:22,717 --> 00:01:27,295
But a tag click starts a fresh view:
planner is now the only filter,

24
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:30,305
and the A4 and unrated planners are back.

25
00:01:30,371 --> 00:01:32,681
So pick a tag first, then narrow.

26
00:01:32,885 --> 00:01:37,231
I want a 2026 planner,
so I'll search for 2026.

27
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:40,256
While there's a search, Sort
switches to Best match,

28
00:01:40,256 --> 00:01:42,400
which puts names that match first.

29
00:01:42,604 --> 00:01:45,764
Its page answers the first
question: will it fit?

30
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:50,715
It lists every size it comes
in, the Paper Pro among them,

31
00:01:50,715 --> 00:01:53,110
and its page count: 1,368.

32
00:01:53,316 --> 00:01:54,986
Then: is it any good?

33
00:01:55,109 --> 00:02:00,459
It averages 4.7 stars, from three
reviews, and anyone can read them.

34
00:02:00,502 --> 00:02:03,942
Mei gave four, and wants dot
grids on the notes pages.

35
00:02:03,979 --> 00:02:06,169
Stars alone can't tell you that.

36
00:02:06,374 --> 00:02:08,654
The author's name links to a profile.

37
00:02:08,757 --> 00:02:13,337
Priya's shows a username, a join
date, and what Priya has published.

38
00:02:13,481 --> 00:02:15,811
That's all: no real name, no email.

39
00:02:16,015 --> 00:02:19,225
Back to Priya's planner,
to add a review of my own.

40
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:23,740
Writing one takes an account: Sign in
to review goes to the sign-in page,

41
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:25,670
and brings me straight back.

42
00:02:28,304 --> 00:02:30,594
Reviews are signed with your username.

43
00:02:30,702 --> 00:02:34,562
The stars are the only required
part; the words are optional.

44
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:37,120
Five stars, and one line about why.

45
00:02:38,528 --> 00:02:43,962
Save review, and the average moves
straight away: 4.8, from four reviews.

46
00:02:44,011 --> 00:02:47,378
The heading now says Your
review: there's one per person,

47
00:02:47,378 --> 00:02:49,341
and saving again replaces it.

48
00:02:49,546 --> 00:02:52,426
One more rule: you can't
review your own work.

49
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:57,497
On your own projects this form never appears,
and the server turns the review away

50
00:02:57,497 --> 00:02:58,170
anyway.

51
00:02:58,373 --> 00:02:59,903
Now, taking it home.

52
00:03:00,052 --> 00:03:04,432
Download all variants renders every
edition right here in the browser,

53
00:03:04,432 --> 00:03:06,122
and hands over one zip.

54
00:03:06,249 --> 00:03:10,834
For this planner, that's three
editions of 1,368 pages each,

55
00:03:10,834 --> 00:03:13,071
so it takes a few seconds.

56
00:03:14,336 --> 00:03:18,213
Inside, there's one PDF per
variant, named after it.

57
00:03:18,345 --> 00:03:20,185
The Paper Pro one is mine.

58
00:03:20,390 --> 00:03:25,632
Here's that one in a PDF reader: the same
linked planner, at my tablet's size.

59
00:03:27,048 --> 00:03:30,163
Version history lists the
versions Priya published,

60
00:03:30,163 --> 00:03:32,428
newest first, each with its note.

61
00:03:32,523 --> 00:03:35,123
Saves that were never
published don't appear.

62
00:03:35,329 --> 00:03:41,029
Open in editor on the older one puts that
exact version in my editor, as a new tab.

63
00:03:41,104 --> 00:03:45,261
Like any Open in editor copy,
it's mine, with no link back.

64
00:03:45,468 --> 00:03:48,418
That's a planner found,
checked and taken home.

65
00:03:48,565 --> 00:03:52,085
Next time: what happens when two
people change the same thing.
